{"title":"Ward Coordinator Roadmap","role":"Ward Coordinator","summary":"A Ward Coordinator supports the smooth administrative and operational functioning of a hospital ward. The role coordinates patient movement, documentation, appointments, communication between clinical teams, bed allocation, discharge processes, supplies, and ward records.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Physician Assistant"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Ward Coordinator supports the smooth administrative and operational functioning of a hospital ward. The role coordinates patient movement, documentation, appointments, communication between clinical teams, bed allocation, discharge processes, supplies, and ward records."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Allied Health graduate, this can be a strong entry route into hospital administration and clinical operations. The role is primarily coordination-focused rather than independent clinical practice."},{"type":"h","text":"Key responsibilities:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Coordinate daily ward activities"},{"text":"Support admission, transfer, and discharge processes"},{"text":"Maintain patient and ward documentation"},{"text":"Coordinate with doctors, nurses, technicians, housekeeping, pharmacy and billing teams"},{"text":"Track bed availability and patient movement"},{"text":"Coordinate investigations and procedures"},{"text":"Monitor ward supplies and equipment requests"},{"text":"Assist with patient/family communication"},{"text":"Maintain operational reports and dashboards"},{"text":"Support quality, safety and infection-control processes"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Focus","Key Capabilities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Healthcare foundation"},{"text":"Medical terminology, com